From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:47:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/35] H19: cap the standard-handler key at 16 bytes for
 revision 4 and earlier

The file key of revisions 2-4 is a prefix of a 16-byte MD5 output, but
decryption_key_rev1234 sliced hash[..Length / 8], once inside the 50-round
loop and once for the returned key. Any /Length above 128 bits (V 2 or V 4
with /Length 136 or 256, or V 5 paired with /R 3 or lower, which forces 256)
therefore panicked with a range error inside Document::from_bytes.

Clamp the byte length to 16 so such files open and decrypt with the 16-byte
key, as pdf.js does, instead of panicking. A /Length of 128 bits or less is
unchanged.

The test builds R2 and R3 documents with precomputed O, U and an RC4
content stream; the 121-byte fuzz input is committed as a regression.

Fixes internal #119
---
 hayro-syntax/src/crypto/mod.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hayro-syntax/src/crypto/mod.rs b/hayro-syntax/src/crypto/mod.rs
index 2d407ad..59e1bfe 100644
--- a/hayro-syntax/src/crypto/mod.rs
+++ b/hayro-syntax/src/crypto/mod.rs
@@ -458,6 +458,11 @@ fn decryption_key_rev1234(
     permissions: u32,
     id: &[u8],
 ) -> Result<Vec<u8>, DecryptionError> {
+    // The key is a prefix of a 16-byte MD5 output, so no /Length can yield
+    // more than 16 bytes. Slicing by an out-of-range /Length (V 2 or V 4 with
+    // more than 128 bits, V 5 paired with revision <= 4) used to panic; clamp
+    // as pdf.js does so such files open instead.
+    let byte_length = byte_length.min(16);
     let mut md5_input = vec![];
 
     // TODO: Convert to PDFDocEncoding.
